    "SQL:tombstone-reaping",
    "D-cursor-opaque-token",
    "D-page-cap-and-checkpoint-boundary"
  ],
  "context": {
    "client_id": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-c10000000001",
    "notes": [
      "the step-2 bootstrap closes the checkpoint at '1'; steps 4 to 6 insert e2 (seq 2), delete e1 (seq 3), and insert e3 (seq 4)",
      "the step-7 pull from the checkpoint '1' with limit 2 returns e2 and the e1 tombstone with has_more true and the continuation cursor '1:3': the transfer's start checkpoint '1' and the position '3' (D-cursor-opaque-token; D-page-cap-and-checkpoint-boundary)",
      "the step-9 reap runs the tombstone reaper: every tombstone recorded so far is reaped and the reap horizon rises to 3, the highest reaped seq (SQL:tombstone-reaping)",
      "the step-10 pull from '1:3' answers CHECKPOINT_EXPIRED on an empty page that echoes the cursor (I-8, D-signal-excludes-page-data): expiry checks the start '1', which the horizon has passed, even though the position '3' is not below it, because a transfer expires as soon as the horizon passes the checkpoint it started from (D-cursor-opaque-token)",
      "the engine drops the staged page and keeps its durable state until it rehydrates: the step-11 assert pins the durable cursor '1', e1 still present, and e2 absent (P:cursor-monotonicity-rebase-and-atomic-checkpoints)",
      "the step-12 rehydration pull from '0' is not expired, because a transfer that started from the bootstrap never expires (D-cursor-opaque-token); the reaper removed the e1 tombstone, so the stream holds only e2 (seq 2) and e3 (seq 4), and that exact fit of limit 2 closes the checkpoint at the horizon's high-water '4' (D-page-cap-and-checkpoint-boundary)",
      "rehydration rebuilds local state from the server snapshot, so the step-13 assert and the postconditions pin the local state equal to the server's: the durable cursor '4', e1 gone although its tombstone only ever rode the dropped step-7 page, and e2 and e3 present (P:cursor-monotonicity-rebase-and-atomic-checkpoints); tombstone TTL coupled to checkpoint expiry is what makes that wipe sound (P:mutations-and-column-masked-conflict-resolution)"
    ],
